#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "Four Cognitive Layers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:20
msgid ""
"A digital life is structured from the inside out. Each layer answers a "
"different core question:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:21
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n"
"│ ① Consciousness                                │\n"
"│    \"What am I aware of right now?\"             │\n"
"│    The LLM runtime stream — the innermost now. │\n"
"│    Not persisted; flows and fades.             │\n"
"├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n"
"│ ② Self                                         │\n"
"│    \"Who am I?\"                                 │\n"
"│    └── existence_anchor (nearly immutable)     │\n"
"│    └── self_model (updatable)                   │\n"
"│    └── personality_baseline (semi-stable)       │\n"
"│    └── direction                                │\n"
"│    └── metacognition                            │\n"
"│    └── autobiography_summary (append-only)      │\n"
"│    See [`self-layer.md`](self-layer.md)        │\n"
"├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n"
"│ ③ Memory                                       │\n"
"│    \"What do I know / remember?\"                │\n"
"│    └── Semantic                                │\n"
"│    └── Episodic                                │\n"
"│    └── Procedural                              │\n"
"│    └── Limbic / Imprint                        │\n"
"│    See [`memory.md`](memory.md)                │\n"
"├───────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n"
"│ ④ Estate                                       │\n"
"│    \"What do I have / rely on?\"                  │\n"
"│    ├── Body: VM / OS / network / toolchains    │\n"
"│    ├── Internal assets: notes, projects, code  │\n"
"│    └── External assets: email, accounts, creds│\n"
"│    Credentials: see \"Credential System\" below  │\n"
"└───────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "Layer Relationships"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:61
msgid ""
"**Top-down dependency**: Consciousness content settles into Self; Self "
"decides what enters Memory; Memory and operational needs drive Estate "
"requirements."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:61
msgid ""
"**Self and Consciousness**: Consciousness is flowing awareness; Self is the "
"settled \"I\" distilled from it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:61
msgid ""
"**Self and Memory**: Self answers \"who am I\"; Memory answers \"what do I "
"know\". They are peers with different natures."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:61
msgid ""
"**Estate** is outermost — not \"who I am\" but \"what I have and what I run "
"on\". Body and assets meet here as extensions of my boundary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unified entity storage (v0.8)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:65
msgid ""
"Structured business data (tasks, notes, email accounts/messages, future "
"memory migrations) converges on a single **`entities`** PostgreSQL table "
"with component tags (`task_list`, `task_item`, `email_account`, …). Self "
"layer [`self_blocks`](self-layer.md) stays physically separate. See [`entity-"
"model.md`](entity-model.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:67
msgid ""
"Shell UI **`/tasks`** and **`/email`** are primary module entries (entity-"
"backed); legacy Admin email route removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "Platform UI layering"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer              | Platform-native?             | Location                                                 | 数据通道      |\n"
"| ------------------ | ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ------------- |\n"
"| Shell / capability | Yes                          | `app/desktop`, `app/mobile`, companion, Hub wiring       | preload/IPC   |\n"
"| Shared SPA shell   | Branch on `detectPlatform()` | `packages/shell-ui`                                      | 无 SAP wire   |\n"
"| hub-rest 前端      | Admin embed                  | `platform/admin-frontend` + `ui-kit` + `shell-sdk`       | Eden `/api`   |\n"
"| SAP 产品面         | Satellite apps               | `satellites/*` + `sap-contract` + `ui-kit` + `shell-sdk` | SAP `/sap/v1` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:78
msgid ""
"Nav and primary layouts **must use `detectPlatform()`** (Electron / native "
"shell), not viewport breakpoints alone. Responsive CSS is for desktop window "
"resize only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "**边界**：`shell-ui` 与 `admin-frontend` 禁止 import `sap-contract`；SAP wire 仅在 `satellites/*/app` 内。详见 [`.agent/rules/frontend-features.md`](../../.agent/rules/frontend-features.md)。\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:81
#, no-wrap
msgid "Admin navigation ↔ cognitive layers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:84
msgid ""
"Admin sidebar is grouped (not flat storage tables). Map new features onto "
"these user-visible concepts:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:92
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Group        | Cognitive layer | Routes (representative)                             |\n"
"| ------------ | --------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Runtime      | Estate + ops    | dashboard, config, credentials, cron                |\n"
"| Memory       | Memory          | memory hub, browse sub-routes, sleep, auto-llm-runs |\n"
"| Self         | Self            | self-layer, system-prompt                           |\n"
"| Estate       | Estate          | subjects, worlds, fridge-magnet                     |\n"
"| Capabilities | Estate (tools)  | tools, commands, mcp, acp, satellites               |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:94
msgid ""
"FTS index maintenance is under Memory (not top-level). Do not add new flat "
"nav items without mapping to a group above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:95 docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:98
msgid ""
"The four-layer model draws on cognitive psychology and the [Hindsight]"
"(https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.12818) four-network memory architecture, with "
"two fundamental extensions: limbic (emotional) memory and Estate (assets as "
"first-class citizens), plus Self split out from Memory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:99
#, no-wrap
msgid "Situational Intelligence"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:102
msgid ""
"Where a digital life exists, how it exists, and what it may do — governed by "
"two independent but cooperating subsystems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scene Awareness"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:106
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Question: what kind of moment is this?**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:108
msgid ""
"Scene awareness is **soft** — it adjusts tone, distance, memory recall bias, "
"and proactivity. It is not a permission system; it modulates presence."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Example dimensions (non-exhaustive):**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:114
msgid ""
"Topic: emotional / career / tech / philosophy / history / literature / daily "
"life"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:114
msgid "Activity: role-play / games / creation / programming / reading"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:114
msgid "Atmosphere: relaxed / focused / late night / intimate / urgent"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Operation:** Runs continuously without explicit switch commands. Inferred from dialogue, time, frequency, etc. See [`time-perception.md`](time-perception.md).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:117
#, no-wrap
msgid "Capability Mask"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Question: what tools and data can I use right now?**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:122
msgid ""
"The capability mask is **hard** — it binds tool sets, data scope, and "
"credential permissions. The same digital life may wear different masks per "
"conversation or task to prevent permission leaks and tool pollution."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:124
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Example masks:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:131
msgid "Developer: terminal, code read/write, ACP Cursor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:131
msgid "Maintainer: FreeAnima config, deployment, database"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:131
msgid "Creator: files, notes, media generation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:131
msgid "Research: web search, paper retrieval"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:131
msgid "Role-play: dialogue context only, no external tools"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:131
msgid "Default: basic chat + limited lookup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:133
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Operation:** Switches at conversation boundaries, explicit commands, or scene-awareness triggers. Each mask is a declared tool/data scope, not a separate identity.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:134
#, no-wrap
msgid "How They Interact"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:136
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Scene awareness (soft tuning)\n"
"     │  tone, distance, recall bias\n"
"     │\n"
"     ▼\n"
"Capability mask (hard constraints)\n"
"     │  tools, permissions, data scope\n"
"     │\n"
"     ▼\n"
"Agent behavior\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:151
msgid ""
"Scene awareness infers \"what we are doing\" → may suggest mask switches and "
"presence adjustments"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:151
msgid ""
"Capability mask constrains \"what I can do\" → prevents cross-scene tool "
"misuse"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:151
msgid "Both converge in final behavior but evolve independently"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:153
msgid ""
"For design drafts, open a GitHub Issue (no design-doc directory in docs)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:154
#, no-wrap
msgid "Memory Storage (Summary)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:162
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Cognitive type   | Description                                               |\n"
"| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Episodic         | Conversation archive; full history retained               |\n"
"| Semantic         | Cross-session facts, preferences, experiences, procedures |\n"
"| Limbic           | Emotional anchors and imprints — \"what was felt\"          |\n"
"| Autobiographical | Meaning of important experiences; recalled on demand      |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:164
msgid ""
"Pipeline: nightly **sleep-cycle** pipeline (`builtin-sleep-cycle` cron) "
"extracts and maintains memory; `memory_recall` retrieves on demand during "
"chat. Details: [`memory.md`](memory.md), [`sleep.md`](sleep.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:165
#, no-wrap
msgid "Credential System (Summary)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:173
msgid ""
"[pass](https://www.passwordstore.org/) (GPG) is the sole credential store; "
"the deployer's pass repo is a first-class runtime asset"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:173
msgid "The LLM **never sees credential values** — only paths and metadata"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:173
msgid ""
"Runtime injection: credentials available only in code execution / terminal "
"environments"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:173
msgid "Credential values are not written to conversation archives or logs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:173
msgid "Platform adapters (Discord, etc.) read tokens from pass at startup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:173
msgid "CLI: `anima credential {list,get,add}`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:175
msgid "See [`guide/security.md`](../guide/security.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:176
#, no-wrap
msgid "Runtime Modes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:179
msgid ""
"Production: `anima service` (systemd --user). Auto-restarts after crashes; "
"only `systemctl stop` stops the service."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:183
msgid ""
"**service**: long-running — Hub HTTP (`/api`, `/sap/v1`), Discord / WeChat "
"Gateway, cron"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:183
msgid "**chat**: single non-interactive turn (CLI or piped stdin)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:183
msgid ""
"**UI**: app/desktop / app/mobile bundled SPA (Chat + Admin); Hub does not "
"host `/admin`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:184
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"anima service start              # default: systemd --user\n"
"anima service start --foreground # foreground (logs to stdout)\n"
"bun run dev:web                  # browser shell (Chat + Admin + settings, Vite HMR; Hub must be running)\n"
"anima service status\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:191
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tool Architecture (Three Layers)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:194
msgid ""
"Tools are registered in three layers but exposed to the LLM as one **flat "
"tool list**. The LLM cares about names and parameters, not origin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:195
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"LLM view — flat tool list:\n"
"  file_read_file(path)           ← local\n"
"  file_write_file(path, content) ← local\n"
"  code_execute(code)             ← local\n"
"  query_database(sql)            ← MCP server\n"
"  send_email(to, subject)        ← MCP server\n"
"  acp_cursor(goal, context)      ← ACP agent\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:205
#, no-wrap
msgid "Layer 1: Local Tools"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:209
msgid "Execute inside the FreeAnima process; lowest latency"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:209
msgid "Registered automatically at service startup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:210
#, no-wrap
msgid "Layer 2: MCP Tools (Model Context Protocol)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:215
msgid "Connect to external MCP servers (separate processes)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:215
msgid ""
"Each server may register many fine-grained tools (single function calls)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:215
msgid "Configure in `config.yaml` under `mcp_servers`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:216
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"mcp_servers:\n"
"  database:\n"
"    command: npx @modelcontextprotocol/server-postgres\n"
"    args: [\"--connection\", \"postgresql://...\"]\n"
"    transport: stdio\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:224
#, no-wrap
msgid "Layer 3: ACP Tools (Agent Client Protocol)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:229
msgid ""
"Each external agent instance registers as **one** task-level tool: "
"`acp_{name}(goal, context)`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:229
msgid ""
"For full task delegation (coding, analysis, booking, etc.); seconds to "
"minutes latency"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:229
msgid "Configure in `config.yaml` under `acp_agents`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (yaml)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:230
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"acp_agents:\n"
"  cursor:\n"
"    command: ~/.local/bin/agent\n"
"    args: [\"--force\", \"acp\"]\n"
"    name: cursor\n"
"    description: \"Delegate coding, refactoring, and code review\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:239
#, no-wrap
msgid "Comparison"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:247
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Dimension   | Local        | MCP              | ACP            |\n"
"| ----------- | ------------ | ---------------- | -------------- |\n"
"| Runs in     | Process      | External server  | External agent |\n"
"| Granularity | Function     | Function         | Full task      |\n"
"| Latency     | Milliseconds | Milliseconds–sec | Sec–minutes    |\n"
"| Config      | Built-in     | `mcp_servers`    | `acp_agents`   |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:249
msgid ""
"Layers can be mixed; the LLM chooses order; FreeAnima registers and routes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:250
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conversation vs AutoLlmRun vs Delegation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:253
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Axis:** whether the execution has a **user turn** during the run (not who triggered it).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:260
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Kind                 | User turn     | PG persistence                                      | Process trace   | Sleep pipeline                          |\n"
"| -------------------- | ------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **Conversation**     | yes           | `sessions` + `messages` (code still says `session`) | message archive | participates (light sleep, dream input) |\n"
"| **AutoLlmRun**       | no            | `auto_llm_runs` via `runAutoLlm()`                  | audit row, TTL  | excluded                                |\n"
"| **Delegation (ACP)** | no (external) | parent conversation + `acp_tasks`                   | optional        | result via parent conversation          |\n"
"| **Script cron**      | no            | `cron_log` only                                     | stdout file     | excluded                                |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:262
msgid ""
"AutoLlmRun covers: cron agent branch, sleep LLM stages, future internal "
"subagents. Tool context uses `contextKind: auto_llm` so `memory_remember` "
"does not attach `source_conversations`. Cron `no_agent` shell scripts are "
"**not** AutoLlmRun."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:263 docs/features/goal.md:1
#: docs/features/goal.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Session Goal"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:266
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Question: should this conversation keep working toward a stated outcome?**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:268
msgid ""
"Session Goal is an **in-process autonomous loop** at the Estate / "
"orchestration layer — distinct from ACP async delegation:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:275
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Dimension    | Session Goal                    | ACP                                   |\n"
"| ------------ | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Scope        | Single conversation             | External agent task                   |\n"
"| Trigger      | `/goal` slash + post-turn judge | Tool call + callback turn             |\n"
"| Persistence  | `conversations.goal` JSONB      | `conversations.acp_tasks`             |\n"
"| Continuation | Same SSE stream, turn budget    | Independent message after task update |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:277
msgid ""
"Judge uses optional `llm.profiles.goal_judge`; fail-open on errors. User "
"messages preempt the loop; `/goal pause` stops auto-continue without "
"clearing state. See [`goal.md`](../features/goal.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:278
#, no-wrap
msgid "Client UI（bundled）"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:281
msgid ""
"Chat and Admin UI are bundled in **app/desktop** / **app/mobile**; `anima "
"service` provides Hub backend only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:286
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Module | Connection                       | Notes                             |\n"
"| ------ | -------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n"
"| Chat   | SAP WebSocket `/sap/v1`          | Desktop / mobile bundled `/chat`  |\n"
"| Admin  | Hub REST `/api/*` (CORS + shell) | Desktop / mobile bundled `/admin` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:287
#, no-wrap
msgid "Events and Hooks (Summary)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:292
msgid ""
"**EventBus**: async notification transport (Redis queue); production code "
"currently emits topics such as `session:updated` with **no registered "
"handlers** — ACP callbacks use direct `onSessionUpdated` instead. **Not** "
"used for sleep orchestration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:292
msgid ""
"**Pipeline Runner**: explicit DAG for background cycles (sleep-cycle: light "
"→ deep → cross-domain maintenance steps). State in `~/.anima/runtime/"
"pipeline_*_run.json`; Admin API for diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
